  "claim": "An American comedian starred in the original cast of Saturday Night Live and played Lorne Michaels in the sitcom Martin. The comedian also starred on a sitcom where Karen Maruyama had a recurring role.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Garrett Morris. Sentence: Garrett Morris (born February 1, 1937) is an American comedian and actor.\nPage: Garrett Morris. Sentence: He was part of the original cast of the sketch comedy program \"Saturday Night Live\", appearing from 1975 to 1980.\nPage: Garrett Morris. Sentence: He was also in the sitcom \"Martin\" as Stan Winters from 1992-1995.\nPage: Martin (TV series). Sentence: Martin is an American sitcom that aired for five seasons on Fox from August 27, 1992 to May 1, 1997.\nPage: The Jamie Foxx Show. Sentence: The series stars Jamie Foxx, Garcelle Beauvais, Christopher B. Duncan, Ellia English, and Garrett Morris.\nPage: Karen Maruyama. Sentence: She has appeared on television in supporting roles in a number of sitcoms, including recurring characters on \"The Jamie Foxx Show\", \"Strip Mall\", \"Suddenly Susan\", and \"Arrested Development\".",
